# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{schedule.html}, nofooter
==STA3000F: Advanced Theory of Statistics
[../../index.html Wenlong Mou], Department of Statistical Sciences, University of Toronto, Fall 2026

== Schedule
~~~
{}{table}{}
lecture | topic | references | notes ||
09\/11 | Radon--Nikodym derivatives, concentration inequalities and the probabilistic method, decision theory, admissibility and James--Stein estimation, Bayes rules | [https://www.stat.cmu.edu/~larry/=stat705/Lecture2.pdf Larry Wasserman's notes on concentration], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert%E2%80%93Varshamov_bound Gilbert--Varshamov bound] for Hamming packing, Bickel and Doksum 1.3 | [./sta3000f26-lec1.pdf Lecture 1] ||
09\/18 | Bayes and minimax decision rules, duality and admissibility, sufficient statistics, Rao--Blackwellization, factorization theorem, exponential families, introduction to UMVUE | [https://erdogdu.github.io/csc2532/latex/notes_all.pdf Murat's notes, Chapter 1], Bickel and Doksum 3.2, 3.3, Keener 3.2, [https://sites.stat.washington.edu/jaw/COURSES/580s/581/LECTNOTES/ch13.pdf Jon Wellner's notes] | [./sta3000f26-lec2.pdf Lecture 2] ||
09\/25 | complete sufficient statistics and UMVUE, Fisher information, classical and Bayesian Cramér--Rao bounds, local minimax risk | [https://sites.stat.washington.edu/jaw/COURSES/580s/581/LECTNOTES/ch13.pdf Jon Wellner's notes], Keener 3.2, 4.5, 4.6, Tsybakov 2.7.3 | [./sta3000f26-lec3.pdf Lecture 3] ||
10\/02 | local minimax and local asymptotic minimax lower bounds, Neyman--Pearson lemma and likelihood ratio tests, total variation and Pinsker's inequality, Le Cam's two-point method, monotone likelihood ratios and UMP tests | [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/b13794 Tsybakov 2.3, 2.4, 2.7.3], [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-387-93839-4 Keener 12.1--12.3], van der Vaart 8.7 | [./sta3000f26-lec4.pdf Lecture 4] ||
